      "level": 2,
      "content": "PART A: BASIC CONCEPT OF POVERTY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Poverty is a multi-dimensional problem encompassing economic, social, and structural deprivations.",
        "Poverty is broadly categorized into Absolute, Relative, Chronic, and Transient poverty.",
        "The Poverty Line acts as the primary benchmark in India to identify and measure the extent of poverty.",
        "Causes of poverty stem from both economic imbalances (e.g., unemployment) and social factors.",
        "Sustainable poverty alleviation requires both robust economic growth and targeted government welfare measures."
      ],
      "id": "pr9i9do"
    },
